  "method": "Resolved Corvus, Passer, Alectoris, Perdix and Ursidae on the iNaturalist taxa API, then paged research-grade, non-captive observations with photos in the two projects. Ravens are species or subspecies whose name is Corvus corax or whose preferred common name contains the word Raven. Sparrows are species in genus Passer. Partridges are Alectoris and Perdix. Bears are Ursidae except Ursus maritimus. The birds project qualifies without a further keyword. The animals project qualifies only when the description, a tag or an observation field matches albino or leucistic wording, and melanistic-only text is dropped. Observation ids were deduplicated within each group. The pre-registered rule has no refutation from a zero count.",
